60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the options, Candidate D seems very promising. It uses the midwifery staff who have capacity and doesn't rely on outside surgery agreements.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I find Candidate C most appealing. It mirrors the success of the call-back trial by focusing on coordination and reducing readmissions without requiring travel.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,I agree with Midori. Candidate D is the only one that leverages the available staffing slack in midwifery without adding to the ward nursing vacancies.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Candidate B is the only one that generates actual revenue through on-site tariffs. Everything else is just another expense we can't afford.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I am quite worried about Candidate B. More people coming for day rehab will only make the parking and booking situation worse.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I understand the financial concern, but if we choose B, we risk it failing if the staffing isn't there. Candidate D is much more sustainable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, the cost of readmissions is often higher than the tariffs we gain. Candidate C could save the hospital more money in the long run by keeping patients healthy.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, while C is good, D is a more direct use of existing, under-utilized staff. It's the most efficient use of our current human resources.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Efficiency is not the same as solvency. If we keep choosing ""gentle"" programs, we'll be unfunded again in twelve months. Candidate B is the only logical choice.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I feel Candidate D is a lovely idea. It's a focused group, and since it's for new parents, we can perhaps schedule them during the quieter hours.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I think we have a consensus on the risks of B. Between C and D, D is more immediately viable given the staffing review Misaki mentioned.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I still believe the evidence from the call-back trial makes C the most patient-centric choice. We shouldn't ignore what we know works.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I can't support B or C if they risk adding to the ward nursing load. D is the safest and most supportive choice for the staff.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"You're all ignoring the ledger. We are losing money on floor space. If we don't maximize the tariff potential of our on-site areas, we're failing the hospital.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, please remember that a hospital is for healing, not just for the ledger. I believe Candidate D is the most harmonious choice for everyone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I'll vote for D. It balances the staffing capacity, avoids the parking crisis, and doesn't rely on external agreements that take years to sign.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will stick with C. It is the only option that addresses the cycle of buried initiatives by applying a proven method of patient follow-up.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting for D. It's the only option that doesn't put more pressure on the already exhausted ward nursing teams.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,I'll vote for B. I refuse to support another program that will be bankrupt by next year because it generates no income.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I shall vote for D as well. It seems the most peaceful way to grow without breaking the systems we already have.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
